# Build intermediates.
# Directory.Build.props sends them outside the mod folder: they must never end up inside it, since
# the whole folder goes to the Workshop as it is.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Claude Code session settings, local to this machine.
.claude/

# Development environments
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# System
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# RimWorld converts every PNG to a .dds next to it the first time the game loads the mod. They are
# a per-machine cache, regenerated on demand, and none has ever been tracked here. Ignoring them
# keeps them out of git, not out of an upload: Steam sends Mod/ as it stands on disk, so a .dds
# that appears there would ship.
*.dds

# Windows Explorer folder icons. desktop.ini in the root and in Mod/ points at Art/ModIcon.ico and
# Art/Preview.ico, local conversions of the delivered images that make the folders recognisable in
# the file manager. They are not part of the mod, and Mod/desktop.ini would reach the players.
*.ico

# Test evidence: Pickle's -EvidenceDir target and any other report kept on disk for the session that
# reads it. Screenshots, films and Player.log make it grow without bound, so git carries none of it.
# What is worth keeping goes to docs/runs/ as text (see docs/runs/README.md).
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
evidence/
